{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"37419b8263c1f1fc","name":"card_event_take_liberty","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/WinterWar/events/card_event_take_liberty","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"TAKE LIBERTY","text":"Each player shuffles their hand into their deck, then draws 4 cards.","flavorText":"The last major country to join an alliance with Japan during WWII was Thailand. In 1942, after the successful Japanese invasion of Thailand in December 1941 and the subsequent signing of a military alliance, Thailand formally joined the Axis Powers by declaring war on the Allies. While Thailand formally joined the Axis and aligned with Japan, its military contributions to the war effort were relatively limited. However, for the Japanese the alliance was more about securing diplomatic support and a level of control over strategic territory, as their intention was to use Thailand as their military base to invade Burma and Malaya in the future.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_take_liberty","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_take_liberty_title","SourceString":"TAKE LIBERTY","LocalizedString":"TAKE LIBERTY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_take_liberty_text","SourceString":"Each player shuffles their hand into their deck, then draws 4 cards.","LocalizedString":"Each player shuffles their hand into their deck, then draws 4 cards."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_take_liberty_history","SourceString":"The last major country to join an alliance with Japan during WWII was Thailand. In 1942, after the successful Japanese invasion of Thailand in December 1941 and the subsequent signing of a military alliance, Thailand formally joined the Axis Powers by declaring war on the Allies. While Thailand formally joined the Axis and aligned with Japan, its military contributions to the war effort were relatively limited. However, for the Japanese the alliance was more about securing diplomatic support and a level of control over strategic territory, as their intention was to use Thailand as their military base to invade Burma and Malaya in the future.","LocalizedString":"The last major country to join an alliance with Japan during WWII was Thailand. In 1942, after the successful Japanese invasion of Thailand in December 1941 and the subsequent signing of a military alliance, Thailand formally joined the Axis Powers by declaring war on the Allies. While Thailand formally joined the Axis and aligned with Japan, its military contributions to the war effort were relatively limited. However, for the Japanese the alliance was more about securing diplomatic support and a level of control over strategic territory, as their intention was to use Thailand as their military base to invade Burma and Malaya in the future."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/CandidateArtwork/Winter_war/t_japanese_order_b_ww.t_japanese_order_b_ww","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Japanese WW2 poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/TAKE_LIBERTY.TAKE_LIBERTY","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":355.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_take_liberty_photo","SourceString":"Japanese troops storming the beach of Songkhla, Thailand, December, 1941.","LocalizedString":"Japanese troops storming the beach of Songk